{ ...no — the Stafford Gambit. A pawn for rapid development and a minefield of traps. }
4. Nxc6 dxc6
{ Black's structure looks broken; in exchange every piece flies out. } 5. d3
{ Natural, already inaccurate — the main trap line. } 5... Bc5
{ Eyeing f2. The threats write themselves. } 6. Bg5
{ ?? The losing move, played thousands of times online: the pin looks free. }
6... Nxe4
{ ! The knight can't be taken: 7.dxe4 Bxf2+ 8.Ke2 Bg4+ skewers the queen through the king. }
7. Bxd8 { Taking the queen anyway... } 7... Bxf2+ 8. Ke2 Bg4#
{ A pure minor-piece mate while the captured queen watches from d8. The Stafford in one picture: development beats material. }
